{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-exo-31-1","title":"Exodus 31:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Bezaleel and Aholiab are appointed and qualified for the work of the tabernacle. 12 The observation of the sabbath is again commanded. 18 Moses receives the two tables.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-31-2","title":"Exodus 31:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>I have. 33:12,17; 35:30; 36:1; Isa 45:3,4; Mr 3:16-19; Joh 3:27 Bezaleel. 37:1; 1Ch 2:19,20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-31-3","title":"Exodus 31:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>filled. 35:31; 1Ki 3:9; 7:14; Isa 28:6,26; 1Co 12:4-11 the spirit of God.{Ruach Elohim,} rather, \"a spirit of God;\" which is a usual Hebraism, signifying \"an excellent spirit;\" or, as we should now say, \"a distinguished genius for the work he had to perform.\" No man, by course of reading or study, ever acquired a genius of any kind: we call it natural, and say it was born with the man: Moses teaches us to consider it divine. The prophet Isaiah, (ch. 28:24-29,) pointedly refers to this sort of teaching as coming from God, even in the most common and less difficult arts of life. Dark as the heathens were, yet they acknowledged that all talents and the seeds of all arts came from God.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-31-4","title":"Exodus 31:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>25:32-35; 26:1; 28:15; 1Ki 7:14; 2Ch 2:7,13,14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-31-5","title":"Exodus 31:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>28:9-21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-31-6","title":"Exodus 31:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>I have given. 4:14,15; 6:26; Ezr 5:1,2; Ec 4:9-12; Mt 10:2-4; Lu 10:1; Ac 13:2 Ac 15:39,40 Aholiab. 35:34; 36:1 wise hearted. 28:3; 35:10,25,26,35; 36:1,8; 1Ki 3:12; Pr 2:6,7; Jas 1:5,16,17 that they. 37:1-38:31; Nu 4:1-49; 1Ki 6:1-8:66; 2Ch 3:1-4:22; Eze 43:1-48:35</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-31-7","title":"Exodus 31:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>tabernacle. 26:1-37; 27:9-19; 36:8-38 ark. 25:10-22; 37:1-9 furniture. Heb. vessels.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-31-8","title":"Exodus 31:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>the table. 25:23-30; 37:10-16 pure candlestick. 25:31-40; 37:17-24 the altar. 30:1-10; 37:25-28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-31-9","title":"Exodus 31:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>the altar. 27:1-8; 38:1-7 the laver. 30:18-21; 38:8; 40:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-31-10","title":"Exodus 31:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>28:1-43; 39:1-43; Le 8:7,8,13; Nu 4:5-14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-31-11","title":"Exodus 31:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>the anointing. 30:23-33; 37:29 sweet incense. 30:34-38</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-31-13","title":"Exodus 31:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Verily. 20:8-11; Le 19:3,30; 23:3; 25:2; 26:2 a sign. 17; Ne 9:14; Eze 20:12,20; 44:24 that ye may. Le 20:8; 21:8; Eze 37:28; Joh 17:17,19; 1Th 5:23; Jude 1:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-31-14","title":"Exodus 31:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>keep. 20:8; De 5:12-15; Ne 9:14; Isa 56:2-6; 58:13,14; Eze 20:12; 44:24 everyone. Isa 56:2,6; Eze 20:13,16,21,24 doeth. 35:2,3; Nu 15:35</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-31-15","title":"Exodus 31:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>Six days. 17; 16:26; 20:9; 34:21; Le 23:3; Eze 46:1; Lu 13:14 the sabbath. 16:23; 20:10; Ge 2:2; Le 23:3,32; Lu 23:56; Heb 4:9; *Gr: holy. Heb. holiness. whosoever. Nu 15:32-36; Jer 17:24-27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-31-16","title":"Exodus 31:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>a perpetual covenant. Ge 9:13; 17:11; Jer 50:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-31-17","title":"Exodus 31:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>a sign. 13; Eze 20:12,20 six days. Ge 1:31; 2:2,3; Heb 4:3,4,10 and was refreshed.God, in condescension to human weakness, applies to himself here what belongs to man; though it may refer to the delight and satisfaction with which he contemplated the completion of all his works, and pronounced them very good.</p>\n<p>Ge 1:31; Job 38:7; Ps 104:31; Jer 32:41</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-31-18","title":"Exodus 31:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":31,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":31,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>gave. 24:12,18; 32:15,16; 34:1-4,28,29; De 4:13; 5:22; 9:9-11; 2Co 3:3 the finger. 8:19; 32:16; Jer 31:33; Mt 12:28; Lu 11:20; 2Co 3:7,8</p>"}]}